son  i'm a big supporter  of society  redistributing the luck redistributing  the opportunity helping those who had  less luck because if i had more luck  uh there's no reason why i wouldn't give  back  to society or to others therefore i  don't mind paying my taxes i've never  tried to evade paying my taxes it annoys  me that government servants  any organization likes to grow  any organization sees the growth of the  organization as the ultimate goal like  government sees the growth of their  organization rather than looking after  the potential beneficiary as the bigger  goal i've seen this in language  instruction for immigrants where they  are more concerned  with these uh sort of immigrant service  organizations and they're all kind of  looking after each other rather than  you know activities that would simply  benefit the immigrant but might not  benefit the whole immigrant services  industry  however nothing is perfect everything  has imperfections but as a principle the  idea that  we redistribute the opportunity is a  very good thing and this means  unfortunately a higher  level of taxation than many of us would  like there are those who say well i  shouldn't have to pay tax on anything i  earned my money myself and it's all mine  that's not true because you benefit from  a lot of uh the infrastructure in  society schools roads you name it you  benefit from the luck that came your way  yes you responded to that but even the  fact that you were say energetic or  entrepreneurial in a sense is also a  matter of luck that you were born with  those qualities so  i think that we should all want to  contribute back to the society because  it makes it a better society to live in  and i think the ultimate morality is not  religion or some ideology of  whatever ism it amounts to basically  reciprocity  do unto others as you would have them do  unto you so you do things to help others  and others are going to do things to  help you that is it it doesn't matter  what you believe in i don't believe that  religious people are more moral than  atheists atheists can be at least as  moral  as religious people in fact i prefer to  think that if i do  things for other people i do this as a  sense of solidarity to my fellow human  beings and not because i am hoping that  somebody is looking over me up there and  is going to uh you know  treat me better because i did whatever  i'm not into that kind of stuff at all  so that's what i'm looking at as i'm 71  years old enjoying my language learning  enjoying getting into cooking which i  haven't really done at all and now it's  like anything else it's like language  learning it's like starting a new  language as you get into it it becomes  you know la petite home as they say in  french the appetite comes with the  appetite comes with the eating so the  more i do of it the more i'm interested  the more i enjoy now going to the  supermarket now i have a better sense of  which supermarkets are good and which  are not good where they have good  produce not good produce so it just  brings a whole new world which i'm  enjoying and now i gotta run off and  finish preparing dinner but thank you  again for all the uh well wishes for my  birthday and i have i have been doing  some korean it may be only you know a  little bit of listening while cooking  and  reading and linking but i'm not letting  go i'm committed bye for now
 

